The '''Emperor's Tower''' was a [[mooring tower]] located at the uppermost northern hemisphere of the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second Death Star]]<ref name="SWCT">[[Star Wars: Card Trader|''Star Wars'': Card Trader]]</ref> that housed the [[Emperor's Throne Room|throne room]] of [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]].<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> Its design was reminiscent of the [[Jedi High Council|High Council]] spire of the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Commentary">{{Film|VI}} DVD audio commentary</ref> [[Turbolift|Elevators]] allowed transport between the top of the tower and the [[battle station]] below.<ref name="beware" /> The Emperor's Tower was damaged, along with the second Death Star, during the [[Battle of Endor]],<ref name="Episode VI" /> but the structure survived in the oceans of [[Kef Bir]] for many years, storing the [[Emperor's wayfinder]].<ref name="Episode IX" />

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:DarthSidiousLightning-RotJAVA.png|thumb|right|250px|Darth Sidious casts Force lightning upon Luke within the Emperor's Tower.]]
In the earliest incarnation of the story of the [[1983]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']], the Emperor's Tower didn't house the Emperor's Throne Room, but rather the Imperial capital planet [[Had Abbadon]] did.<ref name="ETR Databank">{{DB|location|emperorsthroneroom|Emperor's Throne Room}}</ref>

In an early idea pitched by [[Rick Carter]] for the [[2015]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']], the [[scavenger]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] was to dive underwater into the Death Star II's remains on a junk planet and find a hidden map inside the Emperor's Tower that indicated the location of the remaining [[Jedi]] and where [[Luke Skywalker]] was hiding.<ref name="TFA Art">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]''</ref> This idea was later revisited in [[2019]]'s [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']], in which Rey visits the ruins of the tower to find a [[Emperor's wayfinder|map]] to the location of the resurrected Emperor instead.<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

